nd Drug Administration (FDA) analyzed data from the 2019 and 2020 National Youth Tobacco Surveys\"}\n   ]}\n ],\n \"methods_quotes\": [\n   {\"loc\": \"text\", \"q\": \"Prevalence, with 95% confidence intervals, of current use of seven tobacco products\"},\n   {\"loc\": \"text\", \"q\": \"were estimated using t-tests; p-values <0.05 were considered statistically significant.\"},\n   {\"loc\": \"text\", \"q\": \"Unstable estimates with a relative standard error of >30% or an unweighted denominator of <50 were suppressed.\"},\n   {\"loc\": \"text\", \"q\": \"The relative percent change (RPC) from 2019 to 2020 was calculated.\"},\n   {\"loc\": \"note\", \"q\": \"Data were weighted to account for the complex survey design and to adjust for nonresponse.\"},\n   {\"loc\": \"text\", \"q\": \"Analyses were conducted using SAS-callable SUDAAN (version 11.0.3; RTI International).\"}\n ],\n \"confidence\": \"high\",\n \"uncertain_fields\": [\"outcome_types\"]}\n```", "type": "text"}]}